> David Parkhurst

How about this (untested) code:

xyplot(y ~ x | A * B, data = mydata, groups = C,
       panel = function(x, y, subscripts, groups, ...) {
         panel.superpose(x, y, subscripts, groups, ...)
         panel.abline(0, 1)
       }, layout = c(2, 5))

Here "mydata" is a data.frame with columns "x", "y", "A", "B", and "C".

--sundar

