Message-ID: <6.0.3.0.2.20060727174219.02037798@mail.interchange.ubc.ca>

Hi all --

I'm sure this is a simple question with a simple answer, but I can't find 
anything in the language guide about it (I'm probably looking in the wrong 
places...)

Is there some trick I can use to assign a vector to the last column of a 
data frame without knowing the column's rank?  Something like:

my.data.frame[END] <- new.vector

Thanks!

Sarah

From sarah.henderson at ubc.ca  Fri Jul 28 01:36:44 2006
From: sarah.henderson at ubc.ca (Sarah Henderson)
Date: Thu, 27 Jul 2006 18:36:44 -0700
Subject: Last column problem solved!
Message-ID: <6.0.3.0.2.20060727183418.0205de50@mail.interchange.ubc.ca>

Peter Alspach, Simon Rosenfeld and Christos Hatzis have all offered 
variations on the following theme:

my.data.frame[,ncol(my.data.frame)] <- new.vector

Thanks everyone!

Sarah

