Alan - these are wonderful quotes until this part.  The belief that the 
data can tell you which variables to use, in the absence of penalization 
for discarded predictors, is illusory.  This approach solves absolutely 
no part of the instability problem, due to extreme model uncertainty. 
Put another way, Ye's approach (see below) will show that the effective 
degrees of freedom remains about 300.  Otherwise thanks very much for 
the excellent quotes.

Frank Harrell

